      "description": "Watch Benfica vs Aarhus highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. On August 20, 2026 , the UEFA Europa League stage was set for a compelling clash between Benfica and Aarhus . Both teams entered the arena with high stakes on the line, delivering a match filled with tactical intrigue and individual brilliance. A Lightning Start at the Luz The match ignited almost immediately, with the home side finding their rhythm in the opening moments. In just the 2nd minute, Rafa Silva showcased his clinical edge, slotting the ball home with his right foot to give Benfica an early lead. The early goal set a frantic pace, leading to some heavy challenges. Leandro Barreiro received a yellow card in the 9th minute, followed by Tomas Araujo in the 24th minute after a tactical foul stopped a dangerous counter-attack. Benfica 's persistence paid off again in the 31st minute when Clement Lenglet 's vision allowed Leandro Barreiro to pounce on a loose ball. Barreiro finished with his left foot to double the advantage. However, Aarhus refused to back down. In the 36th minute, Sebastian Joergensen capitalized on an assist from Jacob Andersen , firing a left-footed strike into the net to bring the Danish side back into the contest. The Crucial Penalty Just as the first half drew to a close, a pivotal moment shifted the momentum back toward the hosts. In the 45+2 minute, Benfica was awarded a penalty. Vangelis Pavlidis stepped up to the spot and calmly sent goalkeeper Mads Hedenstad Christiansen the wrong way with a right-footed shot, ensuring the Eagles went into the break with a significant cushion. Tactical Discipline and Closing Out The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to influence the flow. Aarhus introduced Stefen Tchamche and Rasmus Carstensen early on to find an equalizer, while Benfica responded by bringing on Jhon Duran and Andreas Schjelderup to maintain their offensive threat. The game became a battle of wits in the midfield, with fewer clear-cut chances than the opening period. As the clock ticked down, Stefen Tchamche saw yellow for a rough foul in the 83rd minute, symbolizing the frustration of the visitors. Benfica navigated the final stages professionally, introducing Fredrik Aursnes and Jakub Kaminski to solidify the midfield. After five minutes of stoppage time, the referee blew the final whistle, confirming a vital victory for Benfica in their European campaign."
